%% Mathematics: inline and display, rendered to baked SVG outlines via LaTeX.
%%   lmr2svg examples/math/deck.lmr -o math.html
!title Mathematics
!madewith

!slide Inline and display

Inline maths flows with the text: the Gaussian $\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} e^{-x^2}\,dx = \sqrt{\pi}$ sits on the baseline.

A display equation is centred on its own line — here revealed on the next step:

!pause

$ \mu_{a\to x}(x) = \sum_{x_{\partial a}\setminus\{x\}} f_a(x_{\partial a}) \prod_{y\in\partial a\setminus\{x\}} \mu_{y\to a}(y) $

!slide Marks inside maths

Use `\mk{name}{...}` to name a sub-expression for annotation:

$ p(x) = \frac{1}{\mk{z}{Z}} \prod_a \mk{fac}{f_a(x_{\partial a})} $

The mark `z` is the normaliser and `fac` the factor product — see the
annotations example for how to colour and label them.
